course: dictionary
lesson: 10655
title: Places of learning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A university is a place where people study for a degree after they leave school. Some people also do research there, which means careful study to find out new things. «Vets study for about five years or more at university and learn about many different kinds of animal.» The clues are study, years and learn: it is a place of long, serious learning.
explain: The word can also mean the people who belong to the place: the students and teachers. «Some zoos let apes play memory games on touch screens, and in a famous test young chimps remembered flashing numbers faster than university students.» Here the students are the people, not the building. Try your meaning in the sentence: "faster than the students" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look at the words around the word to choose the meaning. In «a university student», it means a person who studies there. In «at university», it means you are studying at that place. In America people often say «college» instead, so the same kind of place can have different names in different countries.
fact: A university is a place of higher learning, which people go to after school.
fact: The word university can mean the building or place, or the people who belong to it.
fact: «Go to university» is the usual way to say it in the UK.
fact: In the USA people often say «college» instead.
fact: Research means careful study to find out new things.
exercise: «Vets study for about five years or more at university and learn about many different kinds of animal.» What is a university? | *A place of higher learning where people study for degrees | A kind of animal | A school for very young children | A shop that sells books
exercise: Tom says the oldest university is in Oxford. Where does Yasmin say the oldest university is? | London | Tokyo | Oxford | *Fez, Morocco
exercise: «In a famous test, young chimps remembered numbers faster than university students.» What does university students mean? | Teachers who work in zoos | Animals who play games | *People who study at a university | Very young children
test: «A university student is busy learning every day.» What is a university student? | A child who has just started school | *A person studying at a university | A teacher at a primary school | A zoo keeper
test: In America people often say a different word for university. What word do they use? | Playground | *College | Nursery | Library
exam: Which sentence uses university correctly? | *She is at university, studying to become a vet. | She ran fast across the university. | The university barked and wagged its tail. | He bought a loaf of bread at the university.
